codemap 9
tour feature-filter-tours
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Type in the filter field at the top of the Tours tab to narrow the list to tours whose name, or the symbol or file of one of their steps, contains the text, case-insensitively; every keystroke re-filters and scrolls the list to its top, and the toolbar shows how many of all the tours match. The reader reaches for it to find one tour by name in a large map without scrolling the whole list, or to find every tour that walks through a function or file. Under a tour listed because of its steps (its name does not match, and it is not the tour being read), the matching steps show as rows with their number, symbol and file; clicking one opens that tour at that step. A group shows only when a tour under it matches, its count is the number of matching tours, and every group is open while the filter holds text (clicks on group rows do nothing then). Removed tours from the map diff are filtered by name only, since their steps are gone. Clearing the field restores the full list with each group's openness as it was.

